.TH AROCTL 1 2026-09-26 "aro 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
aroctl \- query and control a running aro
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aroctl
.RB [ \-j ]
.RB [ \-s
.IR socket ]
.I command
.RI [ args ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B aroctl
talks to a running
.BR aro (1)
over its socket: it lists windows, workspaces and monitors, runs any action
a key binding can, and prints aro's log.
Replies are aligned text for people, or one line of JSON with
.BR \-j ,
for scripts.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B monitors
Every output, its mode, scale and workspaces.
.B outputs
is the same.
.TP
.B workspaces
The workspaces in use or shown on the bar.
.TP
.B windows
Every window;
.B *
marks the focused one.
.TP
.B focused
The focused window; fails if there is none.
.TP
.B reload
Read the config again and print any problems.
.TP
.B subscribe
Print a line for each change until aro exits, for bar modules and scripts:
.RS
.TP
.BI "focus " "id app_id title"
The focused window, or
.B focus -
for none.
.TP
.BI "open " "id app_id title" "\fR, \fPtitle " "id app_id title" "\fR, \fPclose " id
A window appeared, was renamed, or went.
.TP
.BI "moved " "id output workspace"
A window is somewhere new; it follows every
.BR open .
.TP
.BI "workspace " "output workspace" "\fR, \fPlayout " "output workspace name"
A monitor shows another workspace, or its layout changed.
.TP
.BR "monitor add" | remove " \fIname\fP"
A monitor came or went.
.RE
.IP
Empty fields are
.BR - .
With
.BR -j ,
each line is a JSON object with an
.B event
key.
.TP
.BR wallpaper " [" \fIfile\fP | auto | none ]
Show
.I file
(resolved from the current directory), aro's own wallpaper, or nothing.
aro remembers it across reloads and sessions until the config's
.B wallpaper
line changes.
Alone, print what is shown.
.TP
.BI dispatch " action " \fR[\fIargument\fR]
Run an action, written as in a
.B bind
line of
.BR aro (5),
for example
.BR "dispatch workspace 3" ,
.BR "dispatch focus left" ,
.BR "dispatch layout monocle" " or"
.BR "dispatch spawn foot" .
.TP
.B version
aro's version.
.TP
.BR log " [" \-f "] [" \-\-old "] [" \-\-path ]
Print aro's log.
.B \-f
follows it as it is written, into the next session when aro restarts;
.B \-\-old
prints the previous session's, the one that crashed;
.B \-\-path
only prints where it is.
With aro not running, the log file is read directly.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-json
Reply in JSON.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-socket " \fIpath\fP"
The socket to use, instead of
.BR $ARO_SOCKET .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short usage message.
.TP
.B \-\-version
aroctl's own version.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ARO_SOCKET
Set by aro for every program it starts.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 when the command failed or aro could not be reached.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
aroctl -j monitors | jq '.[].name'
aroctl dispatch spawn foot --server
aroctl wallpaper "$(find ~/pictures -name '*.jpg' | shuf -n 1)"
aroctl log -f
aroctl subscribe | while read -r ev rest; do ...; done
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR aro (1),
.BR aro (5)
